  "description": "Reference Policy Enforcement Point (PEP) client for the Solcis Policy Engine. Wraps both transports — the `policy decide` process-exec seam and the `policy serve` framed-TCP daemon — and enforces the decision fail-closed (PROCEED / BLOCK / HOLD). Verifies the signed serve receipt (pin-first Ed25519 + blake3, anti-replay) before honoring a proceed-able decision. Holds no private key.",
